    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0317" n="267" xml:id="pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/478</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-24T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 137, September 13, 10 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d416-f1"/> For Stevens:</p>
                <p>Are the Allies unable to manage erecting shops as you state because 120 Baldwin
                    men sent home? Department has conferred with Felton and both desire full
                    statement of existing conditions at Vladivostok and what you think should be
                    done to meet situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
